Muttering to herself, she grabbed a fresh set of clothes and made her way to the bathroom. The warm water cascaded over her, washing away the lingering traces of the night before. But even as she scrubbed her skin, she couldn’t shake the feeling of David’s phantom touch.<br><br>Once dressed, she went downstairs and began the task her father had assigned—cleaning the entire house. She swept, dusted, scrubbed, letting the monotony of the work distract her.<br><br>Then, as she wiped down a shelf in the living room, her hand paused.<br><br>A picture.<br><br><style>img{
